<rtept lat="52.0058000000" lon="1.1981700000">
<time>2025-09-04T11:43:21Z</time>
<name>Yacht Club to Woolverstone Church</name>
<desc><![CDATA[Keep right for a few paces and then left onto the grass path along the back of the beach. Immediately after passing the yacht club, you'll come to a T-junction with a concrete track. Turn left and follow it as it swings right, passing the distinctive Cat House on the right. The story goes that, in the 18th century, a supporter of the smugglers on the river displayed his stuffed white cat in a window here to let the smugglers know they were safe from customs men's hence the name. 

After passing the double garage for Cat House, turn left down the signed footpath, a fenced grass path with the boatyard/car park to the left and woodland to the right. The path will lead you through a section of woodland and then out into playing fields. Keep ahead to follow the path, staying close to the fence for Woolverstone Church on the left. Follow the fence as it swings left to reach the church entrance on the left.]]></desc>
